// Help for Hyperion's science and industry toolboxes (M492–M505), in help.ts's format (name | syntax | text), kept apart
// so the toolboxes built at the same time on other branches don't edit the same lines.
export const SCIENCES_HELP = `
# Epidemics
sir | [t, y, new] = sir(beta, gamma, [S I R], days, 'Intervention', [from to cut], 'Vaccinate', v) | The SIR epidemic: y's columns are the susceptible, infectious and recovered each day, new the day's new infections. 'Intervention' rows cut transmission by that share between two days; 'Vaccinate' moves that share of S a day to R ('VaccineFrom' a day); 'Mu' births and deaths. Drawn without outputs.
seir | [t, y, new] = seir(beta, sigma, gamma, [S E I R], days, …) | SEIR: the infected wait in E (latent, 1/sigma days) before infecting. Same options as sir.
sirAge | [t, y, new] = sirAge(beta, C, gamma, N, I0, days, …) | SIR by age groups: C(i, j) the daily contacts a person in group i has with group j, N and I0 the groups' sizes and first infected. y is [S1…Sn I1…In R1…Rn].
epiR0 | R0 = epiR0(beta, gamma, C, N) | The basic reproduction number: beta / gamma, or with groups the largest eigenvalue of the next-generation matrix.
epiFinalSize | z = epiFinalSize(R0) | The share of a population ever infected when nothing intervenes: z = 1 − exp(−R0 z).
herdImmunity | h = herdImmunity(R0) | The share that must be immune for an outbreak to shrink: 1 − 1/R0.
fitEpidemic | f = fitEpidemic(cases, N, 'Model', 'SEIR', 'Sigma', 0.2, 'Report', 0.5) | Fits beta, gamma and the first infected to daily new cases (with 95% intervals: f.BetaCI, f.GammaCI, f.I0CI, f.R0CI) (log scale, Levenberg–Marquardt from nine starts): a struct with Beta, Gamma, I0, R0, RMSE and Fitted. 'Report' is the share of infections counted. Drawn without outputs.
epiRt | [R, lo, hi] = epiRt(cases, mean, sd, 'Window', 7) | The reproduction number over time from daily cases (the renewal equation; the serial interval a gamma with that mean and sd, days), with a 95% band. Drawn without outputs.
sirGillespie | [t, I, ever] = sirGillespie(beta, gamma, [S I R], days, 'Runs', 20) | Random outbreaks (Gillespie's exact method, one infection or recovery at a time): I has a column of infectious people per run, ever the number ever infected in each. Small outbreaks can die out by chance (about (gamma/beta)^I0 of them). Drawn against the smooth SIR without outputs.
seihrd | [t, y, new, admitted] = seihrd(beta, sigma, gamma, [S E I H R D], days, 'Hospital', 0.05, 'StayDays', 10, 'Fatality', 0.15, 'Beds', 500, 'FatalityNoBed', 0.5) | SEIR with hospital beds and deaths: that share of the recovering infectious goes to hospital H for StayDays on average, that share of patients dies (D); past Beds patients, those without a bed die at FatalityNoBed. Takes sir's 'Intervention' and 'Vaccinate' too. Drawn without outputs.
# Pharmacokinetics
pkModel | m = pkModel('CL', 5, 'V', 50, 'Q', 10, 'V2', 80, 'ka', 1.2, 'F', 0.8) | A drug model: clearance CL (L/h) and volume V (L); 'Q' and 'V2' add a second (tissue) compartment, 'ka' (1/h) and 'F' are oral absorption and bioavailability; 'Vmax' (mg/h) and 'Km' (mg/L) make elimination saturate; 'Q3' and 'V3' add a third compartment, 'Lag' the hours before a dose by mouth starts to be absorbed. Its HalfLife and Rates are in the struct.
pkSimulate | [t, C] = pkSimulate(m, dose, 'Route', 'oral', 'Every', 12, 'Doses', 6, 'Hours', 96, 'Window', [MEC MTC]) | The blood concentration over time for a schedule of doses: 'Route' 'iv' (a bolus), 'infusion' (with 'Duration', h) or 'oral'; 'Times' for doses at given hours. Drawn without outputs, with the window if given.
pkSteadyState | s = pkSteadyState(m, dose, tau, 'Route', 'oral') | After many doses every tau hours: Cmax, Cmin, Cavg (F·dose / (CL·tau)), the accumulation and the hours to reach 90% (TimeTo90), with the profile t, C.
pkDosingWindow | w = pkDosingWindow(m, MEC, MTC, 'Route', 'oral') | The longest interval and its dose that keep the steady state between the lowest level that works and the highest that is safe, and a practical interval (4, 6, 8, 12, 24 h…) with its dose. Drawn and explained without outputs.
pkNCA | p = pkNCA(t, C, dose, 'Tail', 3) | Non-compartmental analysis of measured levels after one dose: Cmax, Tmax, AUClast, AUCinf, LambdaZ, HalfLife, CL, Vz and MRT.
pkEffect | [E, Ce] = pkEffect(t, C, 'Emax', 100, 'EC50', 2, 'Hill', 1, 'E0', 0, 'ke0', 0.5) | The drug's effect from its levels: E0 + Emax·Cⁿ/(EC50ⁿ + Cⁿ) (Hill n; a negative Emax inhibits). 'ke0' (1/h) puts the effect in an effect site that follows the blood slowly, so the effect lags the level (the loop drawn without outputs).
pkFit | m = pkFit(t, C, dose, 'Route', 'oral', 'Every', 12, 'Doses', 3, 'Compartments', 2, 'F', 1, 'Lag', 0) | Fits a model to measured levels after known doses: CL and V (ka by mouth; Q and V2 with two compartments), on a log scale (proportional error) from non-compartmental starting values. A pkModel struct with RMSE, Fitted and 95% intervals (CLCI, VCI…). Drawn without outputs.
# DNA and proteins
seqcomplement | c = seqcomplement(seq) | The complementary strand (A↔T, C↔G, and the ambiguity letters), same direction.
seqrcomplement | r = seqrcomplement(seq) | The reverse complement: the other strand read 5′ to 3′.
seqreverse | r = seqreverse(seq) | The sequence backwards.
basecount | c = basecount(seq) | How many A, C, G, T (U counted as T) and other letters: a struct.
gcContent | g = gcContent(seq) | The share of G and C among the bases (0 to 1).
nt2aa | p = nt2aa(seq, 'Frame', 1, 'GeneticCode', 2) | Translates DNA or RNA to a protein by the standard genetic code or NCBI's 'GeneticCode' (a number or a name; '*' a stop, 'X' unknown); 'Frame', 'all' gives the three frames in a cell.
findORFs | t = findORFs(seq, 'MinLength', 30) | Open reading frames (ATG to a stop) on both strands, longest first: a table of Strand, Frame, Start, Stop, Length and Protein. Printed without outputs.
nwalign | [score, alignment, start, identity] = nwalign(a, b, 'GapOpen', 8, 'ExtendGap', 2, 'Alphabet', 'AA', 'ScoringMatrix', 'PAM250') | Global alignment (Needleman–Wunsch, affine gaps): BLOSUM62 for proteins, +5/−4 for DNA. The alignment is three lines ('|' same, ':' similar). Printed without outputs.
swalign | [score, alignment, start, identity] = swalign(a, b, …) | Local alignment (Smith–Waterman): the best-matching stretch of each and where it starts.
seqpdist | D = seqpdist(seqs, 'Method', 'jukes-cantor', 'SquareForm', true) | Distances between the sequences in a cell ('jukes-cantor' or 'p-distance'; unequal lengths are aligned first): a row as pdist, or the square matrix.
seqlinkage | tree = seqlinkage(D, 'average', names) | A UPGMA tree from distances: a struct with its Newick text. Drawn without outputs.
seqneighjoin | tree = seqneighjoin(D, 'equivar', names) | A neighbour-joining tree from distances (unequal rates allowed). Drawn without outputs.
plottree | plottree(tree) | Draws a tree from seqlinkage or seqneighjoin, the leaves named.
geneticcode | c = geneticcode(2) | One of NCBI's genetic codes by number or name: its Name, the AminoAcids of the 64 Codons (TCAG order), the Starts and Stops. Without arguments, lists them.
multialign | [aligned, tree] = multialign({s1, s2, s3}, 'ScoringMatrix', 'PAM250', 'GapOpen', 10, 'ExtendGap', 0.5) | Aligns several sequences together (progressive, as ClustalW: pairwise distances, a UPGMA guide tree, then groups aligned as profiles). Prints the alignment with '*' under identical columns without outputs; aligned is a cell of equal-length rows.
seqconsensus | [s, share] = seqconsensus(aligned) | The most common letter in each column of aligned sequences, and the share that agrees.
fastaread | [headers, seqs] = fastaread('file.fasta') | Reads a FASTA file kept in Files (or FASTA text starting with '>'): one output gives a struct of Header and Sequence, two the headers and sequences as cells.
fastawrite | fastawrite('out.fasta', headers, seqs) | Writes sequences as FASTA (70 letters a line), adding to the file if it exists; also takes fastaread's struct.
genbankread | g = genbankread('file.gb') | The first record of a GenBank file kept in Files: LocusName, Definition, Accession, Version, Organism, Sequence, and Features as a table (Type, Location, Gene, Product).
# Chemistry and reactors
odeset | opts = odeset('RelTol', 1e-6, 'AbsTol', 1e-10) | Tolerances for the ODE solvers (ode15s, ode23s).
ode15s | [t, y] = ode15s(@(t, y) f, [t0 tEnd], y0, opts) | Solves a stiff ODE (fast and slow parts together, as in chemistry) by a Rosenbrock 2(3) method with error control; given more than two times, reports at those.
ode23s | [t, y] = ode23s(@(t, y) f, [t0 tEnd], y0, opts) | The same stiff solver as ode15s.
kineticsSim | [t, C, names] = kineticsSim('A + B -> C; C <-> D', k, c0, tEnd) | A reaction mechanism by mass action: one rate constant per one-way reaction, two (forward, backward) per reversible one; c0 in the order the species first appear. Drawn without outputs.
batchReactor | [t, C, names] = batchReactor(mechanism, k, c0, tEnd) | A well-mixed closed vessel: concentrations over time (isothermal).
pfrReactor | [tau, C, names] = pfrReactor(mechanism, k, cin, tau) | A plug-flow reactor at constant density: concentrations along it by residence time V/Q.
cstrReactor | [C, names] = cstrReactor(mechanism, k, cin, tau) | A continuously stirred tank's steady state for each residence time V/Q in tau (one row each).
arrhenius | k = arrhenius(A, Ea, T) | Arrhenius' law k = A exp(−Ea/(R T)): Ea in J/mol, T in kelvin.
arrheniusFit | [A, Ea, R2] = arrheniusFit(T, k) | A and Ea from rate constants at several temperatures (a straight line of ln k against 1/T). Drawn without outputs.
chemEquilibrium | [c, extent, names] = chemEquilibrium('N2 + 3 H2 <-> 2 NH3', K, c0) | The equilibrium of one or more reactions (K = Π c^ν for each), from the starting concentrations.
acidPH | pH = acidPH(Ka, C) | A weak acid's pH at concentration C (mol/L), water's own ions included (Ka = Inf for a strong acid).
molarMass | [M, atoms] = molarMass('CuSO4·5H2O') | Molar mass (g/mol) from the periodic table: brackets, hydrates ('·', '*' or '.') and charges ('SO4^2-'); a cell of formulas gives a row. atoms is a struct counting each element.
elementInfo | e = elementInfo('Fe') | An element by symbol, name or atomic number: Number, Symbol, Name, Weight (IUPAC's standard atomic weight) and Radioactive. Without arguments, lists all 118.
balanceEquation | [coef, text] = balanceEquation('C3H8 + O2 -> CO2 + H2O') | The smallest whole-number coefficients balancing every element and the charge (put spaces around each '+': 'MnO4^- + Fe^2+ + H+ -> …'). Printed without outputs.
polyproticPH | [pH, species, I] = polyproticPH([7.1e-3 6.3e-8 4.5e-13], C, 'Charge', 0, 'Activity', true) | The pH of an acid with one or more protons (or a base: 'Charge', 1 with NH4+'s Ka for ammonia) by the full charge balance; species are the concentrations of each form. 'Activity' uses Davies' coefficients (fair up to I ≈ 0.5).
bufferPH | [pH, I] = bufferPH(Ka, Cacid, Cbase, 'Activity', true) | A buffer of an acid and its sodium salt, solved exactly (not only Henderson–Hasselbalch).
acidSpecies | F = acidSpecies(Ka, pH) | The share of the acid in each form (fully protonated, one proton lost, …) at each pH: one row per pH. Drawn from pH 0 to 14 without outputs.
titrationCurve | [V, pH, Veq] = titrationCurve(Ka, C, Va, Ct, 'Titrant', 'base', 'Charge', 0, 'Volumes', v) | Titrating Va of an acid (or a base, with 'Titrant', 'acid') at C by a strong base or acid at Ct: the pH as titrant is added, and the equivalence volumes. Drawn without outputs.
activityCoeff | g = activityCoeff(z, I) | Davies' activity coefficient at 25 °C for each charge z at ionic strength I (mol/L).
ionicStrength | I = ionicStrength(c, z) | ½ Σ c z² for ions at concentrations c (mol/L) with charges z.
heatedBatch | [t, C, T, names] = heatedBatch(mechanism, A, Ea, dH, c0, T0, tEnd, 'RhoCp', 4180, 'UA', 0, 'Tcool', 300) | A batch reactor with its energy balance: Arrhenius A and Ea (J/mol) per rate constant, ΔH (J/mol, negative gives heat) per reaction, ρCp in J/(L·K), cooling UA per litre in W/(L·K). Shows a runaway; drawn without outputs.
cstrSteadyStates | [T, C, stable] = cstrSteadyStates(mechanism, A, Ea, dH, cin, Tin, tau, 'RhoCp', 4180, 'UA', 0, 'Tcool', 300, 'Range', [280 450]) | Every steady state of a cooled CSTR: where the heat from the reactions meets the heat carried and cooled away (van Heerden's diagram, drawn without outputs), each marked stable or not by the slope test.
rateLawSim | [t, C, names] = rateLawSim(mechanism, @(c) [rates], c0, tEnd) | A batch (or a constant-density PFR at t = τ) with any rate law: the function gets the concentrations c (in the mechanism's order of species) and returns one net rate per reaction. Rate constants in its place give mass action. Drawn without outputs.
lhRate | r = lhRate(k, K, p, n) | Langmuir–Hinshelwood: k Π K_i p_i (the first n species) / (1 + Σ K_i p_i)^n. n = 1: one adsorbed reactant; n = 2: two adsorbed reactants meeting on the surface; the other species only take sites. One row of p per case.
ergunAlpha | [alpha, beta0] = ergunAlpha(G, Dp, phi, mu, rho0, Ac, rhoc, P0) | Ergun's pressure-drop constant α (1/kg of catalyst) from the mass flux G (kg/(m²·s)), particle size Dp (m), void fraction φ, gas viscosity μ (Pa·s), inlet gas density ρ0 (kg/m³), cross-section Ac (m²), catalyst density ρc (kg/m³) and inlet pressure P0 (Pa).
packedBed | [W, F, y, names, C] = packedBed(mechanism, k, F0, W, 'P0', 101325, 'T', 298.15, 'Alpha', 0) | A gas-phase packed bed along the catalyst mass W (kg): molar flows F (mol/s), the pressure ratio y = P/P0 by Ergun's equation, the gas flow growing as moles are made and the pressure falls. k per kg of catalyst, or a rate law @(c) [...]. Stops where the pressure is all but gone. Drawn without outputs.
pitzerActivity | [gamma, phi, aw] = pitzerActivity(salt, m) | Pitzer's equations for one salt in water at 25 °C at molality m (mol/kg): the mean activity coefficient γ±, the osmotic coefficient φ and water's activity. Salts: NaCl, KCl, LiCl, HCl, NaBr, KBr, NaOH, KOH, NaNO3, KNO3, CaCl2, MgCl2, Na2SO4, CuSO4, or a struct with zM, zX, nuM, nuX, beta0, beta1, beta2, Cphi. Without outputs, γ± and φ against molality beside Davies'.
# Neuroscience
hodgkinHuxley | [t, V, gates, spikes] = hodgkinHuxley(I, T, 'Start', 10, 'Stop', 90) | Hodgkin and Huxley's squid axon for T ms: a current I (µA/cm²) from 'Start' to 'Stop' ms (or one value per 0.01 ms step); gates are m, h, n. Drawn without outputs.
lifNeuron | [t, V, spikes] = lifNeuron(I, T, 'Tau', 10, 'R', 10, 'Threshold', -50, 'Reset', -65, 'Refractory', 2) | A leaky integrate-and-fire neuron (mV, ms, nA with R in MΩ), spike times exact within each step. Drawn without outputs.
lifRate | f = lifRate(I, …) | The integrate-and-fire neuron's firing rate (Hz) for each steady current: 1/(t_ref + τ ln((RI + rest − reset)/(RI + rest − θ))).
izhikevich | [t, V, spikes, u] = izhikevich(I, T, 'Type', 'CH') | Izhikevich's neuron: 'RS' regular, 'IB' bursting, 'CH' chattering, 'FS' fast, 'LTS' low-threshold, 'TC' thalamic, 'RZ' resonator, or 'Params', [a b c d]. Drawn without outputs.
izhNetwork | s = izhNetwork(800, 200, 1000) | Izhikevich's random network of excitatory and inhibitory neurons for T ms (1 ms steps): spikes as rows [time neuron]. A raster without outputs.
lifNetwork | [s, V] = lifNetwork(W, I, T, 'Noise', 1, 'Delay', 1) | Integrate-and-fire neurons wired by W (W(i, j) mV that a spike of j adds to i after the delay), each with its current: spikes [time neuron] and the first five voltages. A raster without outputs.
poissonSpikes | s = poissonSpikes(rate, T, n, 'DeadTime', 2) | Random (Poisson) spike times at rate Hz over T ms: a row, or for n trains rows [time train].
spikeTimes | s = spikeTimes(V, t, threshold) | The times V crosses the threshold upwards (0 mV unless given), between samples.
isiStats | s = isiStats(spikes) | Inter-spike intervals: MeanISI (ms), CV (1 Poisson-like, 0 a clock), Rate (Hz) and the ISI list.
fanoFactor | F = fanoFactor(spikes, T, window) | The variance of the spike count over its mean in windows of that many ms.
psth | [rate, edges] = psth(spikes, T, bin, trials) | Peri-stimulus time histogram in Hz (spikes from many trials or neurons as [time trial] rows). Drawn without outputs.
rasterPlot | rasterPlot(spikes, T) | A dot for every spike, neuron by neuron (spikes as [time neuron] rows).
spikeXcorr | [counts, lags] = spikeXcorr(a, b, maxLag, bin) | The cross-correlogram of two spike trains: how often b fires at each lag after a. Drawn without outputs.
cableNeuron | [t, x, V, speed, arrival] = cableNeuron('Length', 1000, 'Diameter', 2, 'Compartments', 101, 'Active', false, 'Current', 0.1, 'At', 1) | A neuron with length: a cable of compartments (µm; Ri Ω·cm, Rm Ω·cm², Cm µF/cm²), passive or with Hodgkin–Huxley channels ('Active', true: the squid giant axon by default, 'Celsius' 18.5), a current in nA into compartment 'At' from 'Start' to 'Stop' ms. V has a row per time; speed is the spike's in m/s. Drawn without outputs.
synapseConductance | g = synapseConductance(spikes, t, 'Rise', 0, 'Decay', 5, 'Gmax', 1) | A synapse's conductance over time from its input spikes: exponential ('Rise' 0), alpha ('Rise' = 'Decay') or two exponentials, each event peaking at 'Gmax'.
stdpWindow | [d, w] = stdpWindow('Aplus', 0.005, 'Ratio', 1.05, 'TauPlus', 20, 'TauMinus', 20) | Spike-timing-dependent plasticity: the weight change for each post − pre delay (ms). Drawn without outputs.
stdpNeuron | [w, rate] = stdpNeuron('Seconds', 100, 'Inputs', 1000, 'Rate', 10, 'Gmax', 0.015, 'Aplus', 0.005) | Song, Miller and Abbott's neuron (2000): a thousand Poisson inputs on conductance synapses learning by STDP; the weights (÷ the maximum) split into strong and weak and the output rate settles. Drawn without outputs.
detectSpikes | [times, waves, thr] = detectSpikes(x, fs, 'Threshold', 4, 'Polarity', 'neg') | Spikes in a (filtered) recording: crossings of 4 × the noise (median |x| / 0.6745), aligned on their peaks; times in seconds, one waveform per row ('Pre' 0.5 and 'Post' 1 ms around the peak).
spikeSort | [times, unit, waves, pcs] = spikeSort(x, fs, 'Clusters', 0) | Spike sorting: detection, three principal components of the waveforms and k-means; 'Clusters' 0 picks how many units by the silhouette. Draws each unit's mean waveform and the components without outputs.
filterRecording | y = filterRecording(x, fs, 'Band', [300 6000], 'Notch', 50, 'Order', 4, 'CommonAverage', false) | Cleans a raw recording before sorting: a Butterworth band-pass run forwards and backwards (no delay), a notch at the mains frequency and its harmonics, and with 'CommonAverage' each sample less the median of the channels (one column per channel). detectSpikes and spikeSort take 'Band' and 'Notch' too.
swcRead | m = swcRead(file) | A neuron's shape from an SWC file (NeuroMorpho's format; a file in Files, or its text): one row per point, [id type x y z radius parent]. Types: 1 soma, 2 axon, 3 dendrite, 4 apical dendrite.
treeNeuron | [t, V, peak, info] = treeNeuron(swc, 'Active', 'none', 'Current', 0.2, 'At', 1, 'Start', 5, 'Stop', Inf, 'Time', 50, 'Synapses', S, 'Record', ids) | A branching neuron from SWC (a file, its text or swcRead's matrix), cut into pieces up to 'MaxLength' µm (20) and solved by Hines' method as NEURON does. 'Active': 'none', 'soma', 'axon' (soma and axon) or 'all' for HH channels; current in nA into SWC point 'At'; 'Synapses' one row per event [id time gmax(nS) rise decay E]; 'Ri' 150 Ω·cm, 'Rm' 20000 Ω·cm², 'Cm' 1 µF/cm². V has a column per recorded point (the soma and the farthest tip by default). Drawn without outputs: the shape coloured by each piece's highest voltage, and the traces.
abfload | [d, si, h] = abfload(file) | An Axon Binary Format 2 file (Clampex 10 and later): d is samples × channels (× sweeps), si the sampling interval in µs, h the rate, sweeps, mode and the channels' names and units. ABF 1 files: save them as ABF 2 in Clampfit first.
nwbRead | s = nwbRead(file) | A Neurodata Without Borders 2 file (.nwb): one field per time series under /acquisition (and /stimulus/presentation), each with Data (samples × channels, in its unit after the file's conversion and offset), Rate, StartTime, Unit and Timestamps when it has them.
# Physics
projectile | [x, y, t, info] = projectile(v0, angle, 'Drag', k, 'Gravity', 9.81, 'Height', h0, 'At', t) | A throw from the ground (or a height): drag k = ½ρ Cd A/m (1/m) slows it by k|v|v. info has Range, MaxHeight, FlightTime and ImpactSpeed. Drawn without outputs (beside the drag-free path), the ball at time 'At'.
pendulum | [t, theta, omega] = pendulum(L, theta0, T, 'Damping', b, 'Spin', w0, 'At', t) | A pendulum without the small-angle shortcut (degrees out). Drawn without outputs beside the shortcut; with 'At' the pendulum itself at that moment.
pendulumPeriod | T = pendulumPeriod(L, theta0, g) | The exact period from rest at theta0 degrees: 4√(L/g) K(sin(θ0/2)), longer than 2π√(L/g) for big swings.
doublePendulum | [t, angles, E] = doublePendulum(L1, L2, theta1, theta2, T, 'Masses', [m1 m2], 'At', t) | Two pendulums hung end to end: chaos (a tiny change in the start, a different motion). Drawn at 'At' with the path so far.
nbody | [t, X, E] = nbody(m, P, V, T, dt, 'G', G, 'Softening', eps, 'At', t) | Bodies under each other's gravity by velocity Verlet (the energy stays bounded): P and V a row per body (2 or 3 columns, SI). X has a row per time, [x1 y1 x2 y2 …]. Drawn without outputs.
chargedParticle | [t, r] = chargedParticle(q, m, E, B, r0, v0, T, dt, 'Relativistic', true) | A charge moving through uniform electric and magnetic fields (the Boris push): circles, helices, drifts; 'Relativistic' near the speed of light (never reaching it). Drawn in 3D without outputs.
stringWave | [x, y] = stringWave(L, c, pluck, h, t, 'Modes', 200, 'Damping', g) | A guitar string plucked at pluck (0–1 of its length) to height h, at time t, by its Fourier modes. Put t on a slider and Sweep it to watch it move.
slitPattern | [I, x] = slitPattern(lambda, d, width, N, D, x) | The light on a screen D away from N slits of that width, d apart (Fraunhofer): fringes inside the single-slit envelope. Drawn without outputs.
waveField | Z = waveField(sources, lambda, f, x, y, t) | Ripples from point sources (rows [x y amplitude phase]) at time t: where they add and cancel. Drawn without outputs.
efield | [Ex, Ey, V] = efield(charges, x, y) | The electric field and potential of point charges (rows [x y q], coulombs, metres) on a grid. Drawn without outputs: equipotentials and the field's direction.
bfield | B = bfield(wire, I, points) | The magnetic field (T) of a current I (A) along a wire given as points [x y z] (m), at each point (rows): Biot–Savart, exact for each straight piece. Without points, draws the wire and its field lines in 3D.
fieldLines | lines = fieldLines(charges, 'Lines', 14, 'Seeds', S) | Electric field lines of point charges (rows [x y z q]) in 3D, from the positive charges to the negative ones; a cell of [x y z] rows. Drawn without outputs.
opticsSystem | [f, bfl, ffl, M] = opticsSystem('f 50; d 20; f 100') | An optical system by ray-transfer matrices: 'd L' free space, 'f F' a thin lens, 's R n1 n2' a spherical surface (R Inf: flat), 'm R' a mirror (R > 0 concave, focal length R/2). Its focal length, back and front focal distances and ABCD matrix; printed without outputs.
rayTrace | [z, y] = rayTrace('d 100; f 50; d 150', 'Heights', [-1 0 1], 'Angles', 0) | Rays through the system: each ray's height after every element. Drawn without outputs, the lenses as bars.
lensImage | [di, m] = lensImage(f, do, ho) | A thin lens's image: distance (negative: virtual) and magnification. Draws the three principal rays without outputs.
gaussianBeam | [z, w, zWaist, wWaist] = gaussianBeam(w0, lambda, 'd 1000; f 200; d 400') | A laser beam with its waist w0 at the start (lengths in one unit, λ too): its radius through the system (d, f and m elements) and where it focuses after the last.
lorentzTransform | [ctp, xp] = lorentzTransform(beta, ct, x) | Events seen from a frame moving at β = v/c: ct' = γ(ct − βx), x' = γ(x − βct).
velocityAdd | w = velocityAdd(u, v, c) | Adding speeds relativistically: (u + v)/(1 + uv/c²) (c defaults to the speed of light in m/s).
relativistic | s = relativistic(m, v) | A mass m (kg) at speed v (m/s): Beta, Gamma, Energy, RestEnergy, Kinetic (J) and Momentum.
minkowskiDiagram | minkowskiDiagram(beta, events) | A spacetime diagram: the rest frame's axes, the moving frame's (tilted toward the light lines) and events given as rows [ct x], with their coordinates in the moving frame printed.
schrodinger1D | [E, psi] = schrodinger1D(x, V, 'Mass', 1, 'States', 5) | The lowest bound states of a particle in the potential V (eV) on an even grid x (nm), mass in electron masses: energies (eV) and wave functions (columns, ∫ψ² dx = 1). Drawn without outputs, each ψ on its level.
finiteWell | E = finiteWell(V0, width, 'Mass', 0.067) | The bound-state energies (eV) of a square well V0 deep (eV) and width wide (nm), solved exactly.
tunneling | T = tunneling(E, V0, width, 'Mass', 1) | The chance of getting through a rectangular barrier V0 high (eV) and width wide (nm) at each energy E, below or above it. Drawn without outputs.
transmission | [E, T] = transmission(x, V, 'Mass', 0.067, 'Energies', E) | Transmission through any potential sampled on x (nm), by transfer matrices: double barriers show resonant tunnelling. Drawn without outputs.
rigidBody | [t, w] = rigidBody([I1 I2 I3], w0, T) | A body spinning freely (Euler's equations): spin about the middle axis and it tumbles (the tennis-racket effect). Drawn without outputs; energy and angular momentum are printed as checks.
collide1d | v = collide1d(m1, m2, u1, u2, e) | Velocities after a head-on collision with restitution e (1 elastic, 0 sticking together).
diskCollisions | [pos, vel, hits] = diskCollisions(n, 'Box', [10 10], 'Time', 10, 'Radius', 0.3, 'Restitution', 1, 'At', t) | n hard disks bouncing in a box, collision by collision (exact times): positions at 'At' (a slider animates it), velocities and how many hits. Drawn with trails without outputs.
rigidRotation | [t, w, q, axis, L] = rigidRotation(I, w0, T, 'Orientation', [1 0 0 0], 'Gravity', 0, 'Points', 1000) | A body turning in 3D with its orientation kept as a quaternion [w x y z]: principal moments I, body rates w0. 'Gravity' is m·g·l for a top on a fixed point, its centre of mass l along the body's third axis (precession and nutation). axis is that third axis in space, L the angular momentum in space. Drawn without outputs: the path of the axis's tip.
lensAberration | [h, LSA, focus] = lensAberration(lens, aperture) | Real rays (exact Snell's law) parallel to the axis at heights up to the aperture radius: where each crosses the axis against the paraxial focus (spherical aberration), and the paraxial focus at the blue F, yellow d and red C lines when the lens rows give Abbe numbers. lens: one row per surface [radius thickness index] or [radius thickness nd Vd] in mm, Inf for flat.
spotDiagram | [pts, rms, centroid] = spotDiagram(lens, aperture, angle, 'Defocus', 0, 'Wavelength', 587.56, 'Rings', 10) | Where rays filling the aperture land on the paraxial image plane (moved by 'Defocus' mm), at a field angle in degrees; the RMS spot radius in mm.
realRayTrace | realRayTrace(lens, aperture, angle) | Draws a fan of real rays through the lens's surfaces to the paraxial image plane.
schwarzschildOrbit | [x, y, shift, weak] = schwarzschildOrbit(rClosest, rFarthest, orbits) | An orbit round a black hole (or any mass), in units of GM/c² (the horizon at 2): u'' = 1/L² − u + 3u². shift is how far the closest point moves each orbit (radians) against the weak-field 6πGM/(c²a(1 − e²)). Refused inside the last stable orbits.
lightBending | [deflection, captured] = lightBending(b) | Light passing a black hole at impact parameters b (GM/c²): caught when b < 3√3, otherwise bent by the deflection (radians; 4GM/(c²b) when far). Drawn without outputs.
perihelionShift | d = perihelionShift(a, e, M) | General relativity's advance of the perihelion per orbit (radians) for semi-major axis a (m), eccentricity e and central mass M (kg): Mercury's adds up to 43″ a century.
wavePacket | [t, P] = wavePacket(x, V, 'X0', x0, 'K0', 2, 'Sigma', s, 'Times', t, 'Step', 0.05, 'Mass', 1) | A Gaussian wave packet moving in time (Crank–Nicolson, ψ = 0 beyond the grid): x in nm, V in eV, times in fs, K0 the wave number (1/nm), Sigma the spread of |ψ|². P has |ψ|² at each time, one row per time. Drawn without outputs: |ψ|² over x and time, and the last moment.
schrodinger2D | [E, psi] = schrodinger2D(x, y, V, 'States', 4, 'Mass', 1) | The lowest states of a 2D potential (eV on a grid in nm, ψ = 0 beyond it): V as meshgrid makes it (rows follow y) or a function @(x, y). psi is ny × nx × states. Solved by LOBPCG with a sine-transform preconditioner.
schrodinger3D | [E, psi] = schrodinger3D(x, y, z, V, 'States', 4, 'Mass', 1, 'View', '3d') | The same in 3D (up to 40 × 40 × 40): V ny × nx × nz or @(x, y, z); psi ny × nx × nz × states. Drawn without outputs in 3D: where ψ is ±30% of its peak (blue +, orange −); 'View', 'slice' draws the middle z slice instead.
rigidShapes | [t, P, info] = rigidShapes(shapes, pos, vel, 'Box', [10 10], 'Time', 5, 'Gravity', 9.81, 'Restitution', 0.5, 'Friction', 0.3, 'Rolling', 0, 'Density', 1, 'Mass', m, 'Fixed', idx, 'At', t) | Shapes of any kind (dents too: they're split into convex parts by themselves) that fall, bounce, spin and rub in a box: shapes a cell array of n × 2 corners (up to 64, in order round the outline), [w h] boxes or radii (circles); pos rows [x y angle°], vel rows [vx vy spin rad/s]. 'Rolling' resists circles rolling (a coefficient: about 0.01 for a tyre on a road). 'Fixed' shapes stay put (ramps, pegs). P has [x y angle°] of each shape at each t; info the contacts and energy. Drawn without outputs ('At' with a slider animates it).
rigidShapes3D | [t, P, info] = rigidShapes3D(shapes, pos, vel, 'Box', [10 10 10], 'Time', 4, 'Gravity', 9.81, 'Restitution', 0.4, 'Friction', 0.4, 'Rolling', 0, 'Density', 1, 'Mass', m, 'Fixed', idx, 'At', t) | Solids in 3D that fall, bounce, tumble and rub in a box (z up): shapes a cell array of radii (balls), [w d h] boxes n × 3 corners (the solid around them, up to 64), or a cell of parts glued into one solid with dents (each part n × 3 corners or a box [w d h x y z], all in one frame; convexSplit(V, F) makes them from a mesh); 'Rolling' resists balls rolling and any shape rocking or tumbling on an edge or corner; pos rows [x y z] or [x y z rx ry rz] (a turn about r, its length in degrees); vel rows [vx vy vz] or with a spin [… wx wy wz] (rad/s). P has [x y z qw qx qy qz] of each at each t (position and orientation as a quaternion). Drawn lit without outputs.
kerrRadii | R = kerrRadii(a, q, g) | A spinning black hole's radii (units of GM/c², spin a from 0 to 1, electric charge q and magnetic charge g with a² + q² + g² ≤ 1, Kerr–Newman): Horizon, InnerHorizon, Ergosphere (in the equator), ISCOPrograde / ISCORetrograde (the innermost stable circular orbits), PhotonPrograde / PhotonRetrograde (light's circles).
kerrOrbit | [x, y, z, info] = kerrOrbit(a, p, e, inclination, 'Orbits', 5, 'Charge', 0, 'Magnetic', 0, 'ParticleCharge', 0) | An orbit round a spinning black hole (Kerr; G = c = M = 1): size p, eccentricity e, tilt in degrees (over 90° against the spin). info has E, Lz, Carter's Q, PeriapsisShift and NodeShift (degrees an orbit: the frame dragging turns the orbit's plane), t and r. 'Charge' puts a charge q on the hole (Kerr–Newman), 'ParticleCharge' a charge per mass on the orbiting body (it then feels the hole's electric and magnetic fields too; with 'Magnetic' a charged body is pushed off the equator onto a cone). Drawn in 3D without outputs.
kerrLight | [deflection, captured] = kerrLight(a, b, 'Charge', 0, 'Magnetic', 0, 'Inclination', 90, 'Beta', 0) | Light in a spinning black hole's equator at impact parameters b (GM/c²; positive goes with the spin, negative against): light going with the spin gets closer before it's caught. Deflection in radians from 200 GM/c² out and back. Drawn without outputs. With 'Inclination' (degrees from the spin axis) or 'Beta', the rays come from a distant observer there, b and Beta being where each lands in their picture (α, β): traced back in 3D, [captured, closest] out.
kerrShadow | [alpha, beta] = kerrShadow(a, inclination, 'Charge', q, 'Magnetic', g) | The edge of a spinning black hole's shadow seen from far away, inclination degrees off its spin axis (Bardeen's formula): flattened and shifted on the side turning towards you. A charge shrinks it. Several spins drawn together without outputs.
convexSplit | parts = convexSplit(V, F, 'Parts', 16, 'Tolerance', 0.02, 'Search', false) | Cuts a closed solid with dents (a mesh: corners V, n × 3, and faces F, each row the corner numbers of one face, as patch takes them) into convex parts by itself, for rigidShapes3D: each cut is the plane of a face beside a dent, or the plane through the dent's fold that halves its angle (the cut across a bend), that wastes the least (when no single cut helps, as on a pyramid pushed into a cube, the one whose two halves can then be cut best), until every part's hull is at least 98% solid and has at most 64 corners; smooth curved meshes (a ring, a doughnut) come out within a few per cent of their own volume. 'Parts' is the most it makes (up to 32). 'Search', true also tries free planes where the dents' own cuts do poorly (across the part at a quarter, half and three quarters, then the best one tilted and slid): sometimes a closer fit, a few times slower. 'Search', 'full' also looks one cut ahead at every cut, then merges neighbouring parts while their joint hull stays solid (V-HACD's last step): fewer parts (a half ring 12 instead of 14), about five times slower. 'Search', 'voxel' chooses cuts as V-HACD does: the solid chopped into small cubes, and the planes across the axes whose two sides leave the fewest empty cubes in their hulls (every eighth layer first, then layer by layer round the best), judged exactly beside the dents' own cuts, then merged as 'full' does: fewer parts on blocky solids, a few times slower. parts is a cell of n × 3 corners.
kerrDisc | [I, g, r, T, S, lam, E, X] = kerrDisc(a, inclination, 'Pixels', 100, 'Outer', 20, 'Inner', isco, 'Thickness', 0, 'Opacity', 1, 'Colour', 'brightness', 'Temperature', 10000, 'Absorption', 0, 'Scattering', 0, 'Transfer', 'slab', 'Corona', [kTe tau], 'Charge', 0, 'Magnetic', 0) | A glowing disc of gas round a spinning black hole as it would look, ray traced one light ray a pixel: bent over the top and under the hole, a bright ring near the shadow, the side coming towards you brighter (Doppler beaming). I is the brightness (Novikov–Thorne's shape times g⁴), g each pixel's light shift, r where its ray met the disc (NaN for no disc), T the colour temperature seen in kelvin. 'Thickness' (height over radius, up to 0.3) makes it a flaring slab, solid with glowing walls (its inner edge lit by the gas just behind it); 'Opacity' under 1 lets light through it, so the far side and the thin ring of light round the hole shine through (a thick one glows and dims all through its gas, so light skimming through a long stretch of it is dimmed more and the near side shadows the far side); 'Colour', 'temperature' paints each pixel the colour of the light that reaches it, each bit of gas a hot body at its own temperature shifted by g ('Temperature' the hottest gas); 'Absorption', p makes the gas take light by colour, its opacity going as frequency^−p in the gas's own frame ('Opacity' holds at the gas's own peak colour): the gas then also glows most at the colours it takes most (Kirchhoff), so 2, like hot gas (free–free), glows redder while the light from behind comes through bluer, and −1, like dust, the other way; 0 (the default) takes every colour the same. 'Scattering', w (0 to 0.99) is the share of that opacity that turns light aside instead of taking it (electrons in hot gas): the gas must then be hotter to give out its light, so the colours harden (the colour correction, ×1.2 at 0.9, ×1.5 at 0.99), and a see-through disc dims where light is turned away from you. 'Transfer', 'disc' works out the scattered light in a see-through thick disc from all of its gas (light from the hot inner disc lighting the gas further out, a thin slab letting scattered light escape) instead of each point as in a flat slab ('slab', the default); it takes a moment longer. S is each pixel's spectrum (n × n × 17, arbitrary units) at the wavelengths lam (nm, 380 to 780). E and X are the whole picture's light from 0.001 to 1000 keV (X is E times the flux per keV, arbitrary units; 'Temperature' up to 10⁸ K, as in the discs round stellar black holes); 'Corona', [kTe tau] puts a cloud of hot electrons (kTe in keV, 1 to 1000) of optical depth tau (up to 10) over the disc, boosting part of its light by Compton scattering into a power-law tail up to about kTe (X-rays). Lengths through the gas are as the moving gas measures them. Drawn without outputs.
# Geoscience
seismogram | [x, t, tp, ts] = seismogram(dist, fs, T, 'Vp', 6, 'Vs', 3.5, 'Noise', 0.02) | A made-up seismogram dist km from a quake: P and S waves (Ricker wavelets and their codas) in noise, with their true arrival times. Drawn without outputs.
staLta | r = staLta(x, fs, sta, lta) | The short-term over long-term average of a trace's energy (0.5 s and 10 s unless given): it jumps when a wave arrives.
pickArrival | t = pickArrival(x, fs, 'STA', 0.5, 'LTA', 10, 'On', 4) | The first arrival's time (s): STA/LTA finds it, the AIC picker places it. Drawn without outputs.
locateQuake | q = locateQuake(stations, tp, 'Vp', 6, 'Depth', true) | The epicentre (X, Y km), OriginTime and RMS misfit from P arrival times at stations [x y] km (Geiger's method); 'Depth' also finds the depth. Drawn with the distance circles without outputs.
spDistance | d = spDistance(tsp, vp, vs) | The distance (km) to a quake from its S − P time: tsp·vp·vs/(vp − vs).
localMagnitude | ML = localMagnitude(amp, dist) | Richter's local magnitude from a Wood–Anderson amplitude (mm) at a distance (km), by Hutton and Boore.
distance | d = distance(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2, ellipsoid) | The great-circle angle (degrees) between points; with a radius (e.g. 6371) the length in its units; with [a e] (wgs84Ellipsoid) the length on the ellipsoid (Vincenty).
azimuth | az = azimuth(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2) | The bearing from the first point to the second, degrees clockwise from north.
reckon | [lat, lon] = reckon(lat, lon, arclen, az) | Where you arrive going arclen degrees along a great circle at bearing az.
deg2km | km = deg2km(deg, R) | Degrees of arc to kilometres on the Earth (or a sphere of radius R).
km2deg | deg = km2deg(km, R) | Kilometres to degrees of arc.
wgs84Ellipsoid | e = wgs84Ellipsoid | The WGS84 ellipsoid as [semimajor axis (m), eccentricity].
mapProject | [x, y] = mapProject(lat, lon, 'mercator', 'Origin', [lat0 lon0], 'Radius', R) | Map projections: 'mercator', 'equirectangular', 'lambert' (equal-area) and 'orthographic' (the far side NaN).
ll2utm | [E, N, zone] = ll2utm(lat, lon, zone) | Latitude and longitude to UTM eastings and northings (m) on WGS84.
utm2ll | [lat, lon] = utm2ll(E, N, zone, 'south') | UTM back to latitude and longitude.
fractalTerrain | Z = fractalTerrain(k, 'Roughness', 0.8, 'Relief', 1000) | A made-up landscape of (2^k + 1)² heights (the diamond-square method). Drawn as a contour map without outputs.
slopeAspect | [slope, aspect] = slopeAspect(Z, cell) | Each cell's slope (degrees) and the way it faces (degrees from north); rows run north to south.
hillshade | H = hillshade(Z, cell, 'Azimuth', 315, 'Altitude', 45) | How brightly the sun lights each cell (0 to 1): relief made visible. Drawn without outputs.
# ECG and biosignals (for learning, not diagnosis)
ecgSynth | [x, t, beats] = ecgSynth(fs, T, hr, 'RSA', 0.04, 'Noise', 0.02, 'Wander', 0.2, 'Mains', 0.05) | A made-up ECG (mV): P, QRS and T waves, the beat interval swaying with breathing; baseline wander and mains hum if asked. beats are the true R times.
panTompkins | [idx, times, rr] = panTompkins(x, fs) | QRS detection by Pan and Tompkins (band-pass 5–15 Hz, derivative, square, 150 ms integration, adaptive thresholds, search back): the R peaks and RR intervals (s). Drawn without outputs.
hrvMetrics | h = hrvMetrics(rr) | Heart rate variability from RR intervals (s): HeartRate, MeanRR, SDNN, RMSSD, pNN50 and the LF and HF powers (ms²) with LF/HF.
eegSynth | x = eegSynth(fs, T, [freq amp; …], background) | A made-up EEG (µV): a wandering background plus rhythms (10 Hz alpha unless given).
eegBandPower | [p, rel] = eegBandPower(x, fs) | Delta, theta, alpha, beta and gamma power (Welch's spectrum, 2 s segments) and their shares. Drawn without outputs.
patientMonitor | patientMonitor(ecg, fs, 'SpO2', 98, 'Resp', 15, 'BP', [120 80]) | A bedside-monitor-style view of the last 6 seconds: the ECG with its heart rate, a pleth wave and breathing. For learning, not diagnosis.
wdrc | y = wdrc(x, fs, threshold, ratio, 'Attack', 0.005, 'Release', 0.05, 'Gain', 10) | Wide dynamic range compression: above the threshold (dB re full scale) loudness grows 1/ratio as fast.
hearingAid | y = hearingAid(x, fs, 'Edges', [500 1000 2000 4000], 'Gains', [5 10 20 25 30], 'Threshold', -30, 'Ratio', 2) | A multi-band hearing aid: each band its own gain, all compressed. Drawn without outputs.
# Medical imaging (for learning, not diagnosis)
dicominfo | info = dicominfo('slice1.dcm') | A DICOM file's header: modality, size, pixel spacing, slice position, rescale and window values (patient identifiers are left out).
dicomread | I = dicomread('slice1.dcm') | A DICOM file's pixels as stored (int16 or uint16; frames as pages; colour as rows × columns × 3). Reads uncompressed, deflated, big-endian, RLE and JPEG (baseline, 12-bit extended, lossless) files; not JPEG-LS or JPEG 2000.
dicomwrite | dicomwrite(I, 'slice1.dcm', 'Modality', 'CT', 'RescaleIntercept', -1024, 'PixelSpacing', [0.5 0.5], 'ImagePositionPatient', [0 0 z]) | Saves a greyscale image as a DICOM file (16-bit stored values) in Files.
dicomreadVolume | [V, spacing] = dicomreadVolume('slice') | Every slice*.dcm file (or a cell of names) as one volume in Hounsfield units (rescale applied), sorted by position, with [dy dx dz] in mm.
ctWindow | J = ctWindow(I, 'lung'), ctWindow(I, centre, width) | CT values seen through a window (0 to 1): 'brain', 'subdural', 'stroke', 'soft', 'abdomen', 'liver', 'lung', 'mediastinum', 'bone'. Drawn without outputs.
headPhantom | [V, spacing] = headPhantom(n, slices) | A made-up head CT in Hounsfield units (skull, brain, ventricles and a small lesion) to practise on.
orthoSlices | orthoSlices(V, [row col page], spacing, 'Window', 'brain') | Axial, coronal and sagittal slices through a point of a volume, at their true proportions.
regionGrow | mask = regionGrow(V, [row col page], tol) | The connected region around a seed whose values are within tol of the seed's (6-connected in 3D).
segmentHU | [mask, mL] = segmentHU(V, [low high], 'Largest', true, 'Spacing', [dy dx dz]) | Voxels between two HU values (the largest connected part by default) and their volume in millilitres.
# Finance: pricing
blsprice | [call, put] = blsprice(S, K, r, T, sigma, q) | Black–Scholes prices of European options: spot S, strike K, continuous rate r, T years, volatility sigma, dividend yield q (0 if left out).
blsdelta | [dc, dp] = blsdelta(S, K, r, T, sigma, q) | How much the call and put move per unit of the spot.
blsgamma | g = blsgamma(S, K, r, T, sigma, q) | How fast delta changes with the spot (the same for calls and puts).
blsvega | v = blsvega(S, K, r, T, sigma, q) | The change in price per unit of volatility (per 1.00, not per 1%).
blstheta | [tc, tp] = blstheta(S, K, r, T, sigma, q) | The change in price per year as time passes (usually negative).
blsrho | [rc, rp] = blsrho(S, K, r, T, sigma, q) | The change in price per unit of the interest rate.
blsimpv | v = blsimpv(S, K, r, T, value, 'Yield', q, 'Class', 'put') | The implied volatility: the sigma at which Black–Scholes gives the market price (NaN if none does).
binprice | [asset, value] = binprice(S, K, r, T, dt, sigma, flag, q) | A Cox–Ross–Rubinstein tree with American exercise (flag 1 a call, 0 a put): the asset's and the option's value at every node; value(1, 1) is the price.
mcOptionPrice | [price, se] = mcOptionPrice(S, K, r, T, sigma, 'Paths', 1e5, 'Type', 'put', 'Payoff', 'asian', 'Barrier', B, 'Steps', 252) | Monte Carlo prices of European, Asian (average) and knock-out barrier options, with antithetic paths and the standard error.
bondPrice | P = bondPrice(face, coupon, years, yield, f) | A bond's price from its yield (coupons f times a year, 2 unless given).
bondYield | y = bondYield(price, face, coupon, years, f) | The yield to maturity that gives the price.
bondDuration | [mac, mod, conv] = bondDuration(face, coupon, years, yield, f) | Macaulay duration (years), modified duration and convexity: how the price moves with the yield.
zeroCurve | [zero, df, t] = zeroCurve(par, f) | Zero rates and discount factors bootstrapped from par yields at 1/f, 2/f, … years. Drawn without outputs.
nelsonSiegel | y = nelsonSiegel([b0 b1 b2 tau], t) | The Nelson–Siegel yield curve at maturities t.
nelsonSiegelFit | [p, rmse] = nelsonSiegelFit(t, y) | Fits a Nelson–Siegel curve to yields at maturities t. Drawn without outputs.
# Finance: portfolios and risk
tick2ret | R = tick2ret(P, [], 'continuous') | Returns from prices (each column a series): simple (P2/P1 − 1) or continuous (log).
ret2tick | P = ret2tick(R, 'StartPrice', 100, 'Method', 'continuous') | Prices from returns.
ewstats | [mu, C] = ewstats(R) | Each column's mean return and the covariance of the columns.
portstats | [risk, ret] = portstats(mu, C, W) | Each portfolio's risk (standard deviation) and expected return; W has a row of weights per portfolio.
portvrisk | VaR = portvrisk(ret, risk, 0.05, value) | A normal value at risk: the loss exceeded with that probability.
maxdrawdown | [dd, idx] = maxdrawdown(P) | The deepest fall from a peak (a fraction) and where it started and ended.
efficientFrontier | [risk, ret, W] = efficientFrontier(mu, C, n, 'LongOnly', true) | Markowitz's efficient frontier: the least risk for each return, n points, the weights a row each. Drawn with the single assets without outputs.
maxSharpe | [w, ret, risk, sharpe] = maxSharpe(mu, C, rf, 'LongOnly', true) | The portfolio with the best return over the risk-free rate per unit of risk (the tangency portfolio).
valueAtRisk | [VaR, ES] = valueAtRisk(r, 0.99, 'Method', 'historical') | Value at risk and expected shortfall of returns as positive losses: 'historical', 'normal' or 'cornishfisher' (skew and fat tails).
varBacktest | t = varBacktest(r, VaR, 0.99) | Checks a VaR model against what happened: the days lost beyond VaR against the expected number, Kupiec's test and its p-value (reject below 0.05).
garchFit | g = garchFit(r) | A GARCH(1,1) volatility model by maximum likelihood: Omega, Alpha, Beta, the long-run volatility and the daily sigma. Drawn without outputs.
garchSim | r = garchSim(n, omega, alpha, beta) | Returns from a GARCH(1,1) model: calm and stormy spells.
ewmaVol | s = ewmaVol(r, 0.94) | RiskMetrics' exponentially weighted volatility, day by day.
backtestStrategy | b = backtestStrategy(P, 20, 100, 'Cost', 0.001) | A moving-average crossover (in the market while the short average is above the long) against buy and hold: CAGR, volatility, Sharpe, drawdown and trades. Drawn without outputs.
carbonStress | [loss, share, total] = carbonStress(values, emissions, price, 'PassThrough', 0.3, 'Rate', 0.08) | A carbon-price shock: each holding's extra yearly cost valued forever at the rate, as a loss of its value.
carbonStressPath | [loss, share, total] = carbonStressPath(values, emissions, years, prices, 'PassThrough', 0.3, 'Rate', 0.08, 'Decline', 0.03, 'Start', 2026) | A carbon-price path (a row of prices for the years; several rows, several scenarios): each year's cost discounted to the start, emissions falling by 'Decline' a year, the last year's cost going on for ever. Drawn as bars without outputs.
ngfsRead | s = ngfsRead('ngfs.csv', 'Variable', 'Price|Carbon', 'Region', 'World', 'Scenario', 'Net Zero 2050', 'Model', …) | A scenario file in the IAMC format (NGFS's or IPCC's scenario explorer, CSV or Excel) filtered by its columns: a struct with Model, Scenario, Region, Variable, Unit, Years and Values (a row per series).
ngfsHeadline | h = ngfsHeadline | NGFS Phase V's stated range of the global carbon price in Net Zero 2050 (US$2010/t CO₂, 2030 and 2050: Low, High) with its source. Other scenarios: download them from NGFS and use ngfsRead.
# Maths teaching
diffSteps | [d, steps] = diffSteps(f, x) | A derivative worked step by step, each rule named (sum, constant multiple, power, product, quotient, chain, the table), set as real maths. syms x first.
intSteps | [F, steps] = intSteps(f, x, a, b) | An integral worked step by step (linearity, the power rule, the table, a checked substitution), with limits F(b) − F(a).
solveSteps | [x, steps] = solveSteps(eqn, x) | An equation solved step by step: linear ones by moving terms, quadratics by the formula with the discriminant.
rrefSteps | [R, steps, rank] = rrefSteps(A) | Gauss–Jordan elimination with exact fractions, every row operation shown with the matrix after it.
detSteps | [d, steps] = detSteps(A) | A determinant by elimination: the product of the pivots, the sign flipped per swap.
eigSteps | [lambda, steps] = eigSteps(A) | Eigenvalues by the characteristic polynomial det(A − λI) (up to 4 × 4).
tangentLine | tangentLine(@(x) f, x0, [a b]) | A curve with its tangent at x0 and the tangent's equation; put x0 on a slider and watch it slide.
riemannSum | [S, exact] = riemannSum(@(x) f, a, b, n, 'Method', 'mid') | Strips under a curve ('left', 'right', 'mid', 'trap') against the integral. Drawn without outputs.
newtonSteps | x = newtonSteps(@(x) f, x0, n) | Newton's method step by step: a table of x and f(x) and the tangents drawn down to the axis.
taylorPlot | taylorPlot(f, x0, [1 3 5], [a b]) | A function (symbolic) with its Taylor polynomials about x0 of the given orders.
# Semiconductors and materials
siliconNi | ni = siliconNi(T) | Silicon's intrinsic carrier density (cm⁻³) at T kelvin (the band gap by Varshni's law).
pnJunction | j = pnJunction(Na, Nd, 'V', 0, 'T', 300) | A silicon pn junction (doping in cm⁻³) by the depletion approximation: Vbi, the width W and its parts xn, xp (cm), the peak field Emax (V/cm). Draws the band diagram without outputs.
diodeIV | I = diodeIV(V, 'Is', 1e-14, 'n', 1, 'Rs', 0.5, 'T', 300) | Shockley's diode current at each voltage, with series resistance solved exactly. Drawn on a log scale without outputs.
mosfetVth | [Vth, Cox, phiF] = mosfetVth(Na, tox, 'Vfb', -0.9) | An n-MOSFET's threshold from its substrate doping (cm⁻³) and oxide thickness (nm).
mosfetIV | Id = mosfetIV(Vgs, Vds, 'Vth', 0.7, 'k', 2e-3, 'lambda', 0.02) | Square-law drain current (rows by Vds, columns by Vgs); the family of curves without outputs.
materialCurve | [strain, stress, m] = materialCurve('steel', 'aluminium') | Typical stress–strain curves (Ramberg–Osgood, MPa) of 'steel', 'aluminium', 'titanium', 'copper': for teaching, not design data.
tensileTest | t = tensileTest(strain, stress) | From a tensile test: E, the 0.2% offset yield, UTS, the elongation at fracture and the toughness (MJ/m³).
basquinFit | [sf, b] = basquinFit(N, Sa) | Basquin's fatigue line σa = σf′(2N)^b from tested (cycles, amplitude) pairs.
fatigueLife | N = fatigueLife(Sa, 'steel', 'Mean', 50) | Cycles to failure at a stress amplitude (MPa), a mean stress corrected by Goodman.
rainflowCount | c = rainflowCount(x) | Rainflow counting (ASTM E1049) of a load history: rows [range mean count], count 1 or ½. Drawn as a histogram without outputs.
minerDamage | [D, repeats] = minerDamage(c, 'steel', 'Scale', 1) | Miner's rule: the damage of counted cycles (failure at 1) and how many times the history can repeat.
variogramExp | [h, gamma, pairs] = variogramExp(xy, v, lag, nlags) | The experimental semivariogram of samples (rows [x y]) in distance bins. Drawn without outputs.
krigeGrade | [est, var] = krigeGrade(xy, v, query, [nugget sill range]) | Ordinary kriging of grades at the query places with a spherical variogram: the estimate and its variance.
idwGrade | est = idwGrade(xy, v, query, p) | Inverse distance weighting (power p, 2 unless given).
# Agriculture and energy production
et0PM | ET0 = et0PM(Tmin, Tmax, RH, u2, Rs, elevation, latitude, day, 'Sunshine', n) | FAO-56 Penman–Monteith reference evapotranspiration (mm/day): °C, RH a mean % or [RHmin RHmax], wind at 2 m (m/s), Rs in MJ/m²/day (NaN to use sunshine hours), the day of the year.
kcCurve | kc = kcCurve([ini mid end], [ini dev mid late]) | FAO-56's crop coefficient day by day through the four growth stages.
soilWaterBalance | w = soilWaterBalance(ET0, rain, kc, 'TAW', 120, 'p', 0.5, 'Irrigate', true) | The root zone's daily water balance (FAO-56): depletion, stress Ks, crop water use, irrigation whenever the readily available water runs out, drainage. Drawn without outputs.
cropGrowth | g = cropGrowth(Tmin, Tmax, Rs, 'Tbase', 10, 'GDD', 1600, 'RUE', 3, 'HI', 0.5, 'Ks', ks) | A crop on degree-days and intercepted light, slowed by water stress Ks: leaf area, biomass and the yield (t/ha). Drawn without outputs.
economicDispatch | [P, lambda] = economicDispatch(b, c, Pmin, Pmax, demand) | Power stations with costs a + bP + cP² sharing a demand at the least cost: each unit's output (MW) and the system's incremental cost λ.
lcoe | c = lcoe(capex, opex, energy, rate, years, 'Degradation', 0.005) | The levelised cost of energy: capital plus the present value of yearly costs, over the present value of yearly energy.
# Data centres: power demand
dcServer | s = dcServer('Chips', 8, 'Chip', 'gpu1000', 'CPUs', 2, 'Base', 900, 'Fans', 600, 'PSU', W) | An AI server: its accelerators ('gpu700', 'gpu1000', 'gpu1200', 'tpu', 'cpu' or [idle tdp] in W), processors, memory and the rest, fans and power supply. s.Peak is its wall power flat out in 35 °C air.
dcServerPower | [P, parts] = dcServerPower(s, u, 'Inlet', 25) | A server's wall power (W) at accelerator utilisation u (0 to 1) with inlet air at that temperature: parts holds the accelerators, CPUs, base, fans (cube of their speed) and supply losses.
dcWorkload | u = dcWorkload(t, 'Kind', 'training', 'Period', 2, 'Compute', 0.7, 'High', 0.95, 'Low', 0.35, 'Checkpoint', [600 20]) | Utilisation over time (s): a training job's chips in step between computing and exchanging results, idle at checkpoints ([every for] s; 'Start', 'Ramp'); or 'inference' through the day. Drawn without outputs.
dcFacility | f = dcFacility(Pit, Tout, 'Rated', P, 'Supply', 20, 'Approach', 6, 'Carnot', 0.5, 'FanPump', 0.04) | The facility's power from IT power and outside air (°C): UPS, distribution, cooling (a chiller as a share of Carnot's COP, free cooling when the air is cold), other; f.PUE. Drawn as a stack without outputs.
dcCampus | c = dcCampus([year MW; …], years, 'Fill', 18, 'Utilisation', 0.8, 'Climate', [mean season day]) | A campus built in phases, each filling over months: hour by hour, the yearly capacity, peak and mean demand (MW), energy (GWh) and PUE, and the monthly peaks. Drawn without outputs.
dcHeatFlow | q = dcHeatFlow(P, dT, 'air' | 'water') | The flow that carries heat P (W) away at a temperature rise dT: air in m³/s, water in litres a minute.
# Data centres: the grid
dcGridVoltage | [V, taps] = dcGridVoltage(P, Q, 'Source', 1, 'Z', [R X], 'Tap', true, 'Dt', 1, 'Band', 0.01, 'Delay', 30) | The voltage (pu) at a data centre's connection as its load P + jQ (pu, a series one sample every Dt s) changes, fed through R + jX: the exact two-bus solution (NaN past voltage collapse), with an on-load tap changer stepping 0.625% after Delay s outside the band. Drawn without outputs.
dcHostingCapacity | h = dcHostingCapacity([R X], 'PF', 0.98, 'Vmin', 0.95, 'Limit', P) | The most load (pu) a connection hosts before the voltage falls under Vmin (or the thermal Limit), and the nose: the most it could transfer at all. h.LimitedBy says which.
dcFrequency | [df, s] = dcFrequency(t, dP, 'H', 4, 'D', 1, 'R', 0.05, 'Tg', 6, 'F0', 50, 'Battery', [P tau], 'Reserve', P) | The system's frequency deviation (Hz) after the load changes by dP (pu of the system, + more load, − a trip): inertia H, damping D, governors with droop R and lag Tg, a battery's fast response. s holds the nadir, its time, the RoCoF and the settled value. Drawn without outputs.
dcHarmonics | h = dcHarmonics(MVA, kV, Ssc, 'Rectifier', '6pulse', 'Capacitor', MVAr, 'XR', 10, 'Demand', 1, 'Linear', 0.3) | The harmonic currents rectifiers inject ('6pulse', '12pulse', 'afe', 'pfc' or shares of the four) and the voltage distortion through the source and a capacitor bank (its resonance √(Ssc/MVAr), damped by the bus's linear load, a share of the load): THDv, TDD and each harmonic against IEEE 519's limits. Drawn with an impedance scan without outputs.
itic | ok = itic(V, duration) | Whether each voltage event (pu, s) sits inside the ITIC curve IT equipment is built to ride through. Drawn on the curve without outputs.
# Data centres: power converters
dabDesign | d = dabDesign(V1, V2, P, fs, phi) | A dual active bridge (the heart of an 800 V DC solid-state transformer) for power P at switching frequency fs: the turns ratio n for unity voltage gain and the inductance L that carries P at phase shift phi (π/6 unless given); d.Pmax the most at π/2.
dabPower | P = dabPower(V1, V2, n, L, fs, phi) | The power a DAB carries at phase shift phi (rad): V1·nV2·φ(π − |φ|)/(2π² fs L).
dabWaveform | [t, i, w] = dabWaveform(V1, V2, n, L, fs, phi) | The inductor current over one switching period, the current as each bridge switches and whether it switches at zero voltage (w.ZVSPrimary, w.ZVSSecondary), RMS, peak and the power read from the waveform. Drawn without outputs.
dabEfficiency | [eta, loss] = dabEfficiency(V1, V2, n, L, fs, P, 'Rds', [R1 R2], 'Eoff', J, 'Eon', J, 'Ref', [V A], 'Core', W, 'Rac', R) | Efficiency at each power: SiC conduction, switching (turn-on only where it loses zero-voltage switching), core and winding losses. Drawn without outputs.
sstSimulate | r = sstSimulate(d, t, P, 'V1', V, 'C1', F, 'C2', F, 'Ts', 2e-5, 'Bandwidth', [20 300], 'TauI', 5e-4, 'Efficiency', [0.985 0.985], 'Fidelity', 'average') | One solid-state transformer module closed loop against a load P(t) on the 800 V bus: the PFC holding the DC link (the DAB's power fed forward), the DAB holding the bus, both PI controllers sampled every Ts with a one-sample delay, tuned to the bandwidths (r.Kp, r.Ki). 'switching' simulates the inductor current itself. Drawn without outputs.
dcControllerCode | code = dcControllerCode(Kp, Ki, Ts, ref, 'Limits', [lo hi], 'Language', 'c', 'Frac', 16) | The PI controller written out for a processor ('c', floating point) or an FPGA ('verilog', signed fixed point with Frac fractional bits), with anti-windup clamping.
# Data centres: cooling
coolingCompare | c = coolingCompare(IT kW, rack kW, 'Chip', W, 'Dry', T, 'Wet', T, 'FacilityWater', 32, 'Tower', 4, 'Cycles', 4) | Air, single-phase liquid (cold plates) and two-phase cooling compared over the hours of weather given: fans, pumps, chiller and tower (kW), partial PUE, the hottest chip, whether the rack density works, chiller hours and water use (L/h, WUE in L/kWh). Drawn without outputs.
chillerPower | [P, COP] = chillerPower(capacity kW, COP, PLR, Tcond) | A variable-speed chiller's power and COP at part load (0.1 to 1) and condenser water (°C), its rated COP at 30 °C scaled by Carnot's ratio.
pumpPower | P = pumpPower(q, qmax, Pfull, 'Strategy', 'variable', 'Static', 0.2) | A pump's or fan's power by the affinity laws: 'constant' speed with a bypass, 'variable' speed holding a fixed pressure, 'dpreset' following the system curve.
coolingLoop | r = coolingLoop(t, P, 'FacilityWater', 30, 'Setpoint', T, 'Gains', [Kp Ki], 'Pumps', [N spare], 'FailAt', s, 'Fouling', share, 'Control', 'pi', 'Tmax', 85) | A rack's liquid loop through time as its heat P(t) (W) changes: chips, coolant and the CDU (ε-NTU), pump speed by a PI on the coolant (or 'fixed'), a pump failing at FailAt, the exchanger fouling by that share over the run ('R', 'C', 'Mass', 'UA', 'Flow', 'PumpPower', 'MinSpeed'). Drawn without outputs.
hxUA | UA = hxUA(Thot_in, Thot_out, Tcold_in, Tcold_out, mhot) | A heat exchanger's UA (W/K) from measured temperatures and the hot side's flow (kg/s), counterflow log-mean temperature difference.
foulingTrend | f = foulingTrend(t, UA, 0.8) | When to clean a heat exchanger: 1/UA fitted as a straight line (fouling building up) and the time UA reaches that share of clean. Drawn without outputs.
wetBulb | Tw = wetBulb(T, RH) | The wet-bulb temperature (°C) from dry bulb and relative humidity (Stull's fit).
# Data centres: power on site
gasTurbine | g = gasTurbine(x, 'Rated', 50, 'Efficiency', 0.4, 'Ambient', 15, 'Price', 4) | A gas turbine at load share x: efficiency at part load, capacity derated in hot air, heat rate (Btu/kWh), fuel (MMBtu/h), cost ($/h at the gas price per MMBtu) and CO₂ (t/h). Drawn as its part-load curve without outputs.
fuelCell | [V, P, s] = fuelCell(i, 'Type', 'pem', 'Cells', N, 'Area', cm2) | A fuel cell's voltage at current density i (mA/cm²) and the stack's power (kW): ohmic, activation and mass-transport losses ('pem' or 'sofc'); s.Efficiency on hydrogen's lower heating value, s.H2 in kg/h. Drawn without outputs.
gensetStep | [f, s] = gensetStep(t, [time share; …], 'H', 1.2, 'Gains', [Kp Ki], 'Tau', 0.6, 'F0', 60) | An engine generator's frequency as blocks of load land on it: the dip (%), the time back inside the band, and the ISO 8528-5 classes met (G1, G2, G3). Drawn without outputs.
hybridPower | h = hybridPower(load, dt, 'Grid', MW, 'Turbines', [count MW min ramp], 'Battery', [MWh MW efficiency], 'Solar', pv, 'Prices', [gas grid], 'GridCO2', 0.4) | A behind-the-meter plant serving a data centre's load (MW every dt hours): the grid up to its limit, turbines committed and ramped, a battery for the fast swings, solar; unserved and curtailed energy, fuel and grid cost, CO₂, battery cycles and turbine starts. Drawn without outputs.
# Data centres: signal and power integrity
sparamLine | S = sparamLine(f, 'Length', m, 'Z0', 50, 'Dk', 3.7, 'Df', 0.01, 'Width', m, 'Zref', 50, 'Stub', [length share Z0]) | A board trace's S-parameters at the frequencies f (Hz): skin-effect and dielectric loss, any impedance mismatch, and a via stub's quarter-wave notch. S is a struct (Frequencies, Parameters n × n × F complex, NumPorts, Impedance).
sparameters | S = sparameters('channel.s4p') | Reads a Touchstone file (version 1, .s1p to .s4p; MA, DB or RI) from your files, or Touchstone text itself.
rfparam | s = rfparam(S, i, j) | One S-parameter against frequency (complex); rfparam(S, 'sdd21') the differential through response of a 4-port (ports 1, 2 in; 3, 4 out).
touchstoneWrite | txt = touchstoneWrite(S, 'out.s2p') | Writes S-parameters as Touchstone (RI, Hz): to a file in your files, or returned as text.
ctleResponse | H = ctleResponse(f, [dc fz fp1 fp2]) | A continuous-time linear equaliser's response: DC gain (dB), a zero and two poles (Hz).
pulseResponse | [p, t, cursor] = pulseResponse(S, rate, 'SamplesPerUI', 16, 'Rise', s, 'CTLE', [dc fz fp1 fp2]) | The channel's response to one symbol at the symbol rate (t in UI from the main cursor). Drawn with the cursors marked without outputs.
eyeDiagram | e = eyeDiagram(S, rate, 'Modulation', 'NRZ', 'PRBS', 7, 'Swing', 0.8, 'FFE', taps or 'auto', 'CTLE', [dc fz fp1 fp2] or 'auto', 'DFE', 4, 'RJ', UI, 'DJ', UI, 'Noise', V, 'BER', 1e-12, 'Crosstalk', [next fext], 'Mask', [UI V]) | The eye of a high-speed link (NRZ or 'PAM4') through the channel with transmit FFE (zero-forcing with 'auto', 'FFETaps' [pre post]), a CTLE (the best of a sweep with 'auto'), a DFE, jitter, noise and crosstalk: height, width (and at the target BER), the BER, the bathtub, the taps chosen and the mask's verdict. Drawn with its bathtub without outputs.
pdnImpedance | [Z, s] = pdnImpedance(f, 'VRM', [R L], 'Caps', [n C ESR ESL; …], 'Plane', [C R L], 'Die', [C R L], 'Target', ohms, 'Step', [dI rise duration]) | A power distribution network's impedance from the regulator through capacitor groups (ESL with their vias) to the planes and the die, its anti-resonance peaks, where it passes the target impedance, and the rail's droop when the load steps. Drawn without outputs.
irDrop | r = irDrop('Size', [W H], 'Grid', [nx ny], 'Copper', oz, 'VRM', [x y w h V; …], 'Loads', [x y w h A; …], 'Voids', [x y w h; …], 'Limit', 3, 'Jmax', A/mm2) | The DC voltage drop and current density across a copper plane (a resistor mesh solved by conjugate gradients): the map, the worst drop, each load's voltage and the cells over the limits. Drawn as a map without outputs.
`;
